@host = http://localhost:8000

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### Start a scoring run for any name: VS Code asks for the name when you send it.
# Resolves the name, then researches in the background.
# Expect 202 {"id": "<slug>", "status": "running"} and a Location header.
# The response is saved as `submit`, so the requests below can reuse its id.
# @prompt person Name of the person to score
# @prompt descriptor Optional descriptor to disambiguate (leave empty for none)
# @name submit
POST {{host}}/score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{person}}",
  "descriptor": "{{descriptor}}"
}

### Poll the latest run started above, using the id saved in `submit`.
# status: running -> done | failed. The report is in `report` once done.
# Needs a 202 from a `submit` request earlier in this VS Code session.
GET {{host}}/score/{{submit.response.body.$.id}}

### Poll any id: VS Code asks for it (the slug from a 202 response)
# @prompt id Run id, e.g. luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva
GET {{host}}/score/{{id}}

### Rerun the latest subject even if it is already done (costs a full research run)
# @prompt person Name of the person to rerun
POST {{host}}/score?refresh=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{person}}"
}

### Ambiguous name: expect 409 with candidates, nothing stored
POST {{host}}/score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Peter Singer"
}

### Disambiguated with a descriptor: expect 202
POST {{host}}/score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Peter Singer",
  "descriptor": "Australian moral philosopher"
}

### Not a public figure: expect 422 with a reason, nothing stored
POST {{host}}/score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Q. Nobody"
}

### Blank name: expect 422 before any model call
POST {{host}}/score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}

### Unknown id: expect 404
GET {{host}}/score/nobody

### The plain chat research agent (unchanged, synchronous, no storage)
POST {{host}}/research
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lula da Silva"
}
